ersonal remarks severity? But we have that they make nasty remarks about colleagues. That's a clear negative. Could be mitigated? Not sure.\n\nC's communication difficulty is also serious for crew coordination. Egocentric and unwilling to further education also negative.\n\nD's hot temper is severe.\n\nThus B might be the best despite memory weakness (which can be mitigated with tools). The nasty remarks are concerning but maybe less severe than communication deficits? Hard to decide.\n\nWe need to produce provisional preference. I think B is a solid candidate: stress handling, conscientious, weather assessment, computer skills. Memory weakness can be mitigated. Interpersonal remarks are a concern but maybe less impact than communication deficits of C and hot temper of D. A's unknown calmness is a bigger unknown.\n\nThus I will provisionally favor Candidate B, but note uncertainties about interpersonal behavior and memory. Also note that if evidence shows A is calm under stress and show-off not detrimental, could shift.\n\nLet's produce public message accordingly."}
