ent under pressure, decision-making, teamwork/communication, professional development.\n\nLet's score roughly:\n\n- Reliability/responsibility: A (leadership, anticipation) moderate; B (very conscientious, takes responsibility) high; C (100% reliable) high; D (takes responsibility seriously) high.\n\n- Technical competence: A (spatial vision, complex connections) high; B (weather assessment, computer) moderate-high; C (understands complicated tech) moderate; D (problem solving, concentration) moderate.\n\n- Calmness under pressure: A unknown; B handles stress well; C keeps calm in crisis; D responds adequately but hot temper.\n\n- Decision-making: A anticipates dangerous situations (proactive), sees connections; B maybe; C makes correct decisions quickly; D solves problems extremely well.\n\n- Teamwork/communication: A show-off, not open to new ideas (potentially negative); B nasty remarks (negative); C difficulty communicating, egocentric (negative); D know-it-all, hot temper (negative). All have issues.\n\n- Professional development: A not open to new ideas (negative); B excellent computer skills (positive), but maybe not; C not willing to further education (negative); D hot temper (negative). B seems best.\n\nThus B seems overall balanced: strong reliability, stress handling, technical, but interpersonal negativity. C has calmness but communication issues. D has responsibility but temper. A has strong technical but unknown calmness.\n\nGiven lack of data on A's calmness, which is critical, I might lean toward B as provisional. However B's nasty remarks could be severe for crew cohesion. But we have no data on frequency. Could ask about B's remarks severity? But we have only that they make nasty remarks. That's a clear negative.\n\nC's communication difficulty also severe. D's hot temper also severe.\n\nThus B may be best despite remarks. I will provisionally favor Candidate B, with moderate confidence, noting uncertainties about the impact of his nasty remarks and memory weakness. Also note that if evidence emerges that A is calm under stress and show-off not detrimental, could shift.\n\nNow produce public message summarizing."}
