s => moderate.\n- Technical: understands complicated technology => moderate.\n- Calmness: keeps calm in crisis => good.\n- Decision-making: quick correct decisions => good.\n- Teamwork: difficulty communicating, egocentric => negative.\n- Professional development: not willing to further education => negative.\n\nOverall: good calmness and decision-making, but communication and development issues.\n\nD:\n- Reliability: takes responsibility seriously, responds adequately => moderate-high.\n- Technical: solves problems extremely well, concentration => good.\n- Calmness: hot temper => negative; responds adequately to unexpected events but temper may affect.\n- Decision-making: solves problems extremely well => good.\n- Teamwork: know-it-all, hot temper => negative.\n- Professional development: no info about willingness to learn.\n\nOverall: strong problem solving, but temperament issues.\n\nThus the best candidate likely B or A. A lacks calmness data; B has calmness data. B's interpersonal issue is nasty remarks, but we have no detail. A's show-off may affect crew but unknown.\n\nGiven the weighting, calmness under pressure is critical for long-distance flights. B has explicit evidence. A unknown is a risk. So B seems more reliable.\n\nThus Agent 2 may shift to Candidate B. But we need to consider that other agents (1 and 3) favor B. So aligning may be good.\n\nWe must produce public message summarizing our current preferred candidate, evidence, alternatives, tradeoff, uncertainties, what would change vote.\n\nWe also need to reference that we have no info on A's calmness and show-off impact, and B's remarks lack detail.\n\nWe should also note that we have no further info on C's communication specifics, D's temper severity.\n\nThus we can state we now favor Candidate B, with confidence maybe 70%.\n\nWhat would change our vote? If we get evidence that A is calm under stress and show-off not detrimental, or that B's remarks are severe and impact crew safety, or that C's communication is better than thought, etc.\n\nNow produce output."}
